<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-frostbitten-tremolo" category="High Gain" order="100" instrument="guitar" style="Black Metal">
  <description>Cold, thin second-wave black metal: a parametric metal distortion with the lows cut and the treble up, into a near-clean British head, a 4x12 and a wide, dark hall. Buzzy and icy rather than heavy; made for fast tremolo-picked minor chords and blast beats.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Black Metal</tag><tag>90s</tag><tag>Rhythm</tag><tag>Tremolo Picking</tag><tag>Thin</tag><tag>Reverb</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filosofem" title="Filosofem (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transilvanian_Hunger" title="Transilvanian Hunger (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://equipboard.com/pros/euronymous" title="Equipboard: Euronymous"/>
    <source url="https://forum.metal-archives.com/viewtopic.php?t=75150" title="Metal Archives forum: black metal guitar tone"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
